WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.371 --> 00:00:03.829
- [Man] On 9/11 people
said here's our opportunity

00:00:03.829 --> 00:00:07.451
to help, even though
we knew nobody by name,

00:00:07.451 --> 00:00:10.389
they were all strangers
when they came to Canada.

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:12.106
How the community came together,

00:00:12.106 --> 00:00:14.015
it was an amazing feat.

00:00:14.015 --> 00:00:16.848
(uplifting music)

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.360
- [Narrator] In the moments
after the September 11th

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.645
terrorist attacks, United
States airspace was closed.

00:00:24.645 --> 00:00:27.887
Hundreds of inbound flights
needed a safe place to land.

00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:31.877
One of those places was
Gander, Newfoundland.

00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:34.603
- Once you get halfway across the ocean,

00:00:34.603 --> 00:00:36.594
the closest airport is Gander.

00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:38.395
And at that day, they were told to land

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:40.267
at the nearest airport.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.215
And 38 aircraft was nearer to Gander

00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:46.159
than they were any other airport.

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:49.951
- I get this call, "Get out
in back of the airport."

00:00:49.951 --> 00:00:53.118
So I go up there, and I'm just in awe.

00:00:54.282 --> 00:00:56.896
I watched this big jet come in.

00:00:56.896 --> 00:01:00.619
And I look again, and
there's lights of another one.

00:01:00.619 --> 00:01:01.619
I go oh God.

00:01:03.474 --> 00:01:05.995
- The night the planes landed here,

00:01:05.995 --> 00:01:08.309
I was at the Legion, and the first thing

00:01:08.309 --> 00:01:11.010
come out of my mouth was
thank God they're coming here,

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.772
'cause I know they're
gonna be looked after.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.211
Not saying they wouldn't
be looked after elsewhere,

00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:17.621
but I knew they would
be looked after here.

00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:20.095
- [Narrator] Nearly 7000 shaken
and disoriented passengers

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:22.997
arrived in Gander, almost
doubling the population

00:01:22.997 --> 00:01:25.455
of the tiny Canadian town.

00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:28.037
- A plan of action went
into place, just like that.

00:01:28.037 --> 00:01:30.379
And that's what the whole
community became involved with.

00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:33.474
- I don't know of anybody
who didn't do something,

00:01:33.474 --> 00:01:35.778
be it, you know, something
big or something small.

00:01:35.778 --> 00:01:37.807
Everybody seemed to have done something,

00:01:37.807 --> 00:01:40.085
because you knew it had to be done.

00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:41.813
- [Narrator] All across Gander,
people opened their doors

00:01:41.813 --> 00:01:43.519
to stranded passengers,

00:01:43.519 --> 00:01:46.434
including over 700 at
a local primary school.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:47.634
- The teachers went home that day

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.566
and emptied out their linen closet,

00:01:49.566 --> 00:01:51.989
took every blanket and pillow
that was not on the bed,

00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:54.655
and they brought it back to the school.

00:01:54.655 --> 00:01:58.229
By early morning,
maybe 5 or 6 o'clock,

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:01.793
we had had four flights
arrive at Gander Academy.

00:02:01.793 --> 00:02:03.919
We kinda went on adrenaline.

00:02:03.919 --> 00:02:07.807
I know I didn't go home and
sleep until 72 hours later.

00:02:07.807 --> 00:02:08.971
It just went on for days.

00:02:08.971 --> 00:02:12.306
And everything that we
needed seemed to come.

00:02:12.306 --> 00:02:15.365
And I still don't know how that happened.

00:02:15.365 --> 00:02:18.367
- This is one from a schoolteacher
in Montclair, New Jersey.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.850
He sent me that on the first anniversary.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.410
People invited them into their homes,

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.231
gave them keys to their
cars, the keys to their home,

00:02:25.231 --> 00:02:27.605
and never blinked twice about it.

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:29.083
- [Narrator] The generosity
of the people of Gander

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.802
was a bright spot on one of
the world's darkest days.

00:02:32.802 --> 00:02:35.502
- When it was all over,
I was never more prouder

00:02:35.502 --> 00:02:38.635
that the greatest strength
we have is our people.

00:02:38.635 --> 00:02:41.968
And we have great people here in Gander.

